* The roots of a·x*2 + b·x + c = 0, real or complex.
1.1 Set d = b*2 - 4·a·c.
1.2 To part 2 if d < 0.
1.3 Type c, [-b+sqrt(d)]/[2·a], [-b-sqrt(d)]/[2·a] in form 1.
1.4 Done.

2.1 Type c, -b/[2·a], sqrt(-d)/[2·a] in form 2.

Form 1:
c = ___   real roots     ___.____ and ___.____
Form 2:
c = ___   complex roots  ___.____ plus and minus ___.____ i

Set a = 1.
Set b = -2.
Do part 1 for c = -8, -1, 1, 5.
